00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:29.640
lewis the fish story by arthur urinks pictures by richard igelski

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:40.480
One day last spring, Lewis, a butcher, turned into a fish.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:49.610
Silvery scales, big lips, a tail, a salmon.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:55.020
Lewis did not lead before this an unusual life.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:59.430
His grandfather was a butcher, his father was a butcher.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.710
Lewis was a butcher. He had a small shop on Flatbush. Steady customers, good meat.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:15.360
He was always friendly, always helpful, a wonderful guy. But Lewis was not a

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:22.760
happy man. He hated meat. On birthdays, his beaming parents would hand him a

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:29.320
gift-wrapped salami. When he was 13, they gave him a turkey.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:34.200
Lewis did anything to get away from meat.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:39.460
He got a job afternoons, cleaning fish tanks in a doctor's office.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.110
Lewis loved the job.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:50.390
For hours, he'd stare at the fish, their eyes blinking, their fins flapping.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:56.470
But a good thing doesn't last long.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:07.020
One night, at dinner, Lewis' mother said to his father, "Nat, why does Lewis have to slave

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.990
over those lousy fish? What's the matter? You can't give him a little job in the store?

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:21.750
Ma-Ma, I like..." "You're right, Rose. Tomorrow, Lewis, after school, you come to the store.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:30.000
It's time you learned something about meat." And that was it. Every day, Lewis was at his

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:35.260
Someday, this will all be yours, his father would say.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.060
And it was.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.000
His parents died suddenly, and Lewis took over the butcher shop.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.170
For years, that's where he worked.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.930
Lewis was so unhappy.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.260
His only happy times were when he was in the refrigerator.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.710
There, he'd sit for hours and draw fish.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.000
Big one.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:07.540
little ones. He'd draw them all over the place. Surrounded by stakes, all Lewis

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:20.650
thought about was fish. But then it got worse. He began to see fish everywhere. At

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:30.000
home, on the bus, at ball games. Even his customers began to look like fish to him. Business

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.280
started to fail. His health

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.280
declined. He

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.180
was always thirsty.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:40.380
At night, Lewis had trouble

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.160
sleeping. One night

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.270
in May, he had

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.240
bad dreams.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.890
He dreamt he was walking

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:51.890
down the street and he was attacked.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.000
Hamburgers were

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.000
punching him, salamis

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.010
kicked him, lamb chops,

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.000
roast beefs, and briskets

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:10.340
ganged up on him, yelled for help, but no one came.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:16.550
That morning, Lewis woke up feeling cold and wet.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:22.200
He was a fish, a salmon.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:28.000
Al, from Al's pet store, found him on the bus going up Flatbush.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:34.560
"Look at that face," he tells his customers.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:39.020
"I couldn't eat him, so I brought him to the store."

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:45.720
Lewis soon forgot everything about being a butcher, living on Flatbush, or even being

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:52.000
a human being at all.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:58.710
After a hard life, Lewis was a happy fish.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.230
What a beautiful fish-tale.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:20.820
Not your fish-tale.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:22.620
The tale of Lewis the fish.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:23.620
The story!

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:30.000
That Lewis sure was lucky, he didn't have to flounder

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.290
life as a human. It must be every human's dream. Yeah, I catch adrift. To go to sleep

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:53.070
a person. And wake up a salmon. That's the best fish story I've heard in years.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:56.910
I know Lewis was happy to turn into a fish for the rest of his life. I'd kind of like

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.000
to see the world from a fish's point of view too. But not

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.700
if it meant having to spend every day in a school. Besides, after living for a few days

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:10.030
as a fish, I'd probably like to turn into something else for a little while. Like a

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:15.960
giraffe with a neck so long, I could see way above the treetops. Or maybe even an eagle.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:22.220
They're so majestic, and I've always wanted to fly. If you could be anything in the world,

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:30.000
anything, what would you choose? I would like to be an alligator because it has sharp

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:39.090
they can swim well and it is a green I would choose to be a snake a duck a lion

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:44.490
a hummingbird I would like to be a horse I would like to be a camel because it

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:50.800
has two humps and a camel is my favorite kind of animal a leopard a giraffe a

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:55.450
rabbit a monkey because they swing around on vines and I like to swing

00:09:55.450 --> 00:10:00.000
around on vines I would be a shark because I like the water

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:08.280
I can really see why you would want to be a fish like me.

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:18.440
Living in the ocean is like a fantasy.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:22.640
It's so easy living way down below.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.300
The sea will take you anywhere you want to go.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:30.000
All around can feel the ocean flow.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:11:00.000
Emotion will astound you, there's so much to see, look around, just flow, it's the best way to be from me, out for a week too, and you will surely see, a barracuda or an angelfish, was what you were meant to be.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:11.820
The shark one gets out of your way, and lie on the-

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:15.330
Well, if that's what you wish, he-

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:31.510
See you.

